  "description": "The deployment will run in a clustered mode with the master\u2011slave architecture turned on, providing three slave replicas alongside the master instance. Persistence is enabled for both roles: the master uses a 50\u202fGi persistent volume claim, selected by the label\u202f`role=master` and the expression\u202f`tier=backend`; the slaves each use a 30\u202fGi claim, matching the label\u202f`role=slave` and the expression\u202f`tier=frontend`.  \n\nMetrics collection is active, with a side\u2011car exporter deployed and a Prometheus Operator ServiceMonitor created to scrape the endpoints. Password authentication is required, using the supplied password **A1b2C3d4E5**. Although the configuration supports init\u2011container volume permission handling, this feature is disabled for the current release."
